    "campaign_summary": "A Peruvian integrated digital security alert documents six critical vulnerabilities and two malware campaigns threatening critical infrastructure and enterprises across August 2026. APT Kimsuky conducts spear-phishing campaigns against South Korean and Japanese targets via OneDrive-distributed malware (.LNK files) that deploys PowerShell backdoors and Chrome browser extensions for credential theft and email exfiltration. Critical vulnerabilities in WatchGuard Agent (CVE-2026-57910, CVE-2026-57909), Gitea (CVE-2026-60004), Red Hat Keycloak (CVE-2026-18963), and Comfast CF-N1-S (CVE-2026-77148) allow remote code execution and account compromise at scale, with Gitea already actively exploited by threat actors deploying cryptocurrency miners.",
